      "text": "# NO BUG: `circuit += oracle` is valid Qiskit (it is `QuantumCircuit.__iadd__`, which appends the oracle's instructions onto the same two qubits), and the Deutsch circuit logic (X and H on the ancilla, CNOT oracle for the balanced case, final H, measure qubit 0) is correct.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit import QuantumCircuit, Aer, execute\n\ndef deutsch_circuit(oracle):\n    circuit = QuantumCircuit(2, 1)\n    circuit.x(1)\n    circuit.h(0)\n    circuit.h(1)\n    circuit += oracle\n    circuit.h(0)\n    circuit.measure(0, 0)\n    return circuit\n\ndef constant_oracle():\n    circuit = QuantumCircuit(2)\n    return circuit\n\ndef balanced_oracle():\n    circuit = QuantumCircuit(2)\n    circuit.cx(0, 1)\n    return circuit\n\ncircuit = deutsch_circuit(constant_oracle())\nbackend = Aer.get_backend('qasm_simulator')\nresult = execute(circuit, backend).result()\nprint(result.get_counts())\n\ncircuit = deutsch_circuit(balanced_oracle())\nbackend = Aer.get_backend('qasm_simulator')\nresult = execute(circuit, backend).result()\nprint(result.get_counts())\n```",
